      "date": "1974-03-07",
      "kind": "planning decision",
      "description": "The irregular 7,053.5-square-foot parcel (49.9 feet on Wood Street, 125 feet deep) in an R-2 district was a vacant lot owned by the Government of India. The City Planning Commission unanimously approved, with five conditions, a one-storey building over an eight-car garage as a memorial to the Hindustan Gadar Party, housing a museum and library open to the public two days a week, on a site of particular historic significance to the party.",
